Explanation:

• We first check that the candidate element is either the root or a descendant of it.
• Then we require that the “subject” (the last evaluator) match the element.
• For every earlier evaluator, we “climb” the parent chain until we find an ancestor that matches that evaluator. If we ever hit the root without a match (or run out of ancestors), we return false.
• This prevents candidates from matching if the chain “leaks” outside of the supplied context.

Any solution that implements this “climb until match (but not past root)” strategy is acceptable.

