Below is one acceptable fixed version. In our case the problem turned out to be that in the fixed “extra‐fields” branch the battery value was converted using a factor of 0.1 rather than 0.01 (and likewise in one TLV case – so that a raw value of about 395 is incorrectly converted to 39.5 rather than 3.95). One acceptable fix was to change the battery conversion in the fixed branch and in TLV 0xEE so that they both multiply by 0.01. (Any correct answer that supplies KEY_BATTERY with a value of 3.95 for the failing test is correct.) 

